<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <RootNamespace>Cadence.Sample.ClusteredWorker</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Cadence comes from the local package feed (see ../NuGet.config), built by ../../scripts/pack.ps1.
    A project reference would hide packaging mistakes until the first real publish.

    Cadence.Api is here because §13.6 of the design plan says it has to be: a trigger dispatches in
    the process that received it, so a replica that does not map the API is a replica no trigger can
    reach. Cadence.Dashboard is v0.4's operator UI, over the same options object and the same gate.

    Both storage tiers are referenced and only one is used per run — which of them is decided at
    startup by the connection string the AppHost injected. Referencing both is what lets one worker
    project serve both clustered samples.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Cadence.Core" Version="0.2.*-*" />
    <PackageReference Include="Cadence.Api" Version="0.2.*-*" />
    <PackageReference Include="Cadence.Dashboard" Version="0.2.*-*" />
    <PackageReference Include="Cadence.Storage.Sql" Version="0.2.*-*" />
    <PackageReference Include="Cadence.Storage.Redis" Version="0.2.*-*" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    The document comes from the framework; only the UI needs a package, and its assets are embedded
    rather than fetched from a CDN.

    10.0.11 rather than the 10.0.0 its siblings pin: 10.0.0 resolves Microsoft.OpenApi 2.0.0, which
    restore rejects as a known vulnerability (NU1903).
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi" Version="10.0.11" />
    <PackageReference Include="Swashbuckle.AspNetCore.SwaggerUI" Version="10.2.3" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    The sample's dependency, not Cadence's. SalesReportJob returns a JobResult carrying xlsx bytes
    and a media type; Cadence never learns what a spreadsheet is, which is the point of the
    IJobResultSerializer seam.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="ClosedXML" Version="0.104.2" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    OTLP rather than the console exporter Cadence.Sample.Worker uses. Aspire's dashboard collects
    OTLP from every replica, which is what turns "one run per occurrence" into something visible.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTelemetry.Extensions.Hosting" Version="1.18.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTelemetry.Exporter.OpenTelemetryProtocol" Version="1.18.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
